  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PPDP Volvo/UNIDO Ungdomssyssels&#xe4;ttning inom HDEICV i DRC</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPDP Volvo/UNIDO youth employment in HDIECV in DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention is a Public Private Partnership Development Partnership (PPDP) initiative, implemented by UNIDO in collaboration with Swedish companies Volvo and Epiroc to generate jobs for young people in the heavy industrial equipment and construction sector. utility vehicles (HDIECV) in two (Lualaba and Haut Katanga) provinces out of the 26 in the DRC.

The project aims to promote the development of technical skills among young Congolese men and women (mainly those between the ages of 15 and 35). This will enhance the youth workforce in the HDIECV market.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet &#xe4;r ett s&#xe5; kallat Public Private Development Partnership (PPDP), som genomf&#xf6;rs av FN:s industriutvecklingsorganisation (UNIDO) i samarbete med f&#xf6;retagen Volvo och Epiroc. Syftet &#xe4;r att bidra till ungdomssyssels&#xe4;ttning inom tung industriutrustning och kommersiella fordon (HDIECV) i tv&#xe5; av de 26 provinserna i Demokratiska republiken Kongo (DRK). Ett centralt inslag i projektet &#xe4;r att fr&#xe4;mja kompetensutveckling f&#xf6;r unga m&#xe4;n och kvinnor genom teknisk utbildning och yrkesutbildning (TVET), kompletterad med st&#xf6;djande insatser, f&#xf6;r att d&#xe4;rigenom st&#xe4;rka b&#xe5;de utbud och efterfr&#xe5;gan p&#xe5; ungdomsarbetskraft p&#xe5; HDIECV-marknaden. 

Projektet har en systemf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndrande ansats genom att bidra med en ny sorts yrkesutbildning d&#xe4;r privata akt&#xf6;rer &#xe4;r involverade fr&#xe5;n b&#xf6;rjan och bidrar med egna resurser. Medverkan fr&#xe5;n kongolesiska myndigheter ska g&#xf6;ra att modellen blir k&#xe4;nd, etablerad och &#xe4;ven kan anv&#xe4;ndas i andra sektorer. 

Projektet &#xe4;r planerat f&#xf6;r en period p&#xe5; 5 &#xe5;r, fr&#xe5;n april 2022 till mars 2027, vilket betyder att projektet kommer att forts&#xe4;tta bortom slutdatumet f&#xf6;r den nuvarande svenska regeringens strategi f&#xf6;r DRK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a Public Private Development Partnership (PPDP), implemented by the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) in collaboration with the Volvo Group (Volvo) and Epiroc, to generate youth employment in the Heavy Duty Industrial Equipment and Commercial Vehicle (HDIECV) sector in two out of the 26 provinces in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). A key focus of the project is to promote skills development for young men and women through Technical and Vocational Training (TVET), complemented with related interventions, to thereby strengthen both supply and demand for youth labour in the HDIECV market. 

The project aims for systemic change by showing a new model for vocational training where private actors are involved from the start and also contribute with their own resources. Participation from Congolese authorities will make the model known and established so that it can also be used in other sectors. 

The project is planned for a period of 5 years, from April 2022 until March 2027, which is beyond the current Swedish government strategy for DRC.</narrative>
  </description>
